{"anchor": {"begin": [69, 0, 597.33], "end": [69, 0, 663.33], "env": "definition", "file": null, "head": null, "id": 24, "kind": "approximate", "label": null, "labels": [], "line": null, "number": "6.4", "source_sha256": "7d0509354d5d06c6ee1954d044bccb4efcd55a4bddd7cde36004ff984b466c2c", "statement": "Definition 6.4 (Mean and moment coefficients). A smooth coefficient f = f(R, Z, T, H) belongs to M α if it descends to each applicable common torus with representatives satisfying (6.20), extends smoothly by zero outside the active radial shell, and on X a < X < X b satisfies ∂ θ f = 0, ∀I ∈ N5 0 ∃C j,I , b j,I , d j,I : | ∂ I f | ≤ C j,I ε αS b j,I ∗ ζ δ −d j,I. (6.24)", "title": "Mean and moment coefficients"}, "blockers": [], "class": "proved", "clauses": [], "correspondence": {"by": "Christian Garry (drafted with Claude Code)", "confidence": "medium", "coverage": "partial", "note": "MeanClass is the bound (6.24) on an abstract strip domain, with the powers of S∗ and δ^{−1} merged into one degree, and UnweightedClass plays the role of S_α in (6.25). Descent to common tori with (6.20), ∂θ f = 0 and smooth zero extension outside the shell are not part of these definitions.", "source": "confirmed"}, "decls": {"NavierStokes.WeightedClasses.MemClass": "8f8caa870d21ccef1ba2f18b", "NavierStokes.WeightedClasses.MemClass.mk": "6af6fa760d22830b04279ceb", "NavierStokes.WeightedClasses.StripData": "9124f2e7357ce684be8d2d23", "NavierStokes.WeightedClasses.StripData.delta": "d39ce27ea765f2a01bac9722", "NavierStokes.WeightedClasses.StripData.domain": "5f13c2213a2133370ba859bb", "NavierStokes.WeightedClasses.StripData.epsilon": "c2fc612420b10a7dc37649c0", "NavierStokes.WeightedClasses.StripData.growth": "ba8115fc902ecc491e4c726e", "NavierStokes.WeightedClasses.StripData.mk": "13558bc8407e6a1483c71458", "NavierStokes.WeightedClasses.StripData.slow": "03d5bc7747949df1300f97bf", "NavierStokes.WeightedClasses.StripData.zeta": "3f08087239cac61590ae9e7f", "NavierStokes.WeightedClasses.ma